      <h1><em>Best Bourbon &amp; Whiskey in Austin: Staff Picks</em></h1>
      <p class="article-meta">By the Monarch Liquor team &middot; Updated Sept 2026</p>
    </header>

    <!-- Article Body -->
    <article class="content-section" style="padding-top: 20px;">
      <div class="content-narrow prose">
        <p>Between the two stores, our team pours over (and pours from) a lot of whiskey. These are the bottles we recommend most, organized by budget, plus a whole section on the Texas whiskeys we're proudest to stock. Availability rotates &mdash; if something's not on the shelf, ask and we can usually special order it.</p>

        <h2>Everyday Pours (Under $30)</h2>
        <p>Great whiskey doesn't have to be a splurge. These over-deliver for the price:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Buffalo Trace</strong> &mdash; the workhorse Kentucky bourbon: caramel, vanilla, and a soft finish. Perfect neat or in an Old Fashioned.</li>
          <li><strong>Wild Turkey 101</strong> &mdash; bold, spicy, and 101 proof. The bartender's choice for cocktails that punch through.</li>
          <li><strong>Evan Williams Bottled-in-Bond</strong> &mdash; a white-label sleeper that drinks well above its price tag.</li>
          <li><strong>Old Grand-Dad 114</strong> &mdash; high-proof, high-rye, high value. A staff favorite for Manhattans.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Step-Up Bottles ($30&ndash;$60)</h2>
        <p>The sweet spot of the whiskey wall &mdash; gifts, weekend sippers, and impress-your-father-in-law territory:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Four Roses Single Barrel</strong> &mdash; fruity, spicy, and consistently excellent.</li>
          <li><strong>Woodford Reserve Double Oaked</strong> &mdash; dessert in a glass; double-barreled for extra toffee and dark fruit.</li>
          <li><strong>Russell's Reserve 10 Year</strong> &mdash; a decade of age at a price that still feels friendly.</li>
          <li><strong>Rittenhouse Rye Bottled-in-Bond</strong> &mdash; if you're rye-curious, start here.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Special Occasion (Over $60)</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Blanton's Single Barrel</strong> &mdash; the famous horse-topper. When we get an allocation, it goes fast; ask us to keep an eye out for you.</li>
          <li><strong>Angel's Envy Port Finish</strong> &mdash; bourbon finished in port casks; plush, sweet, and dangerously drinkable.</li>
          <li><strong>WhistlePig 10 Year Rye</strong> &mdash; a benchmark rye with big baking-spice character.</li>
        </ul>

