        <h2>Texas Whiskey Worth Seeking Out</h2>
        <p>This is the section we care about most. Texas whiskey has grown up fast, and the Hill Country heat ages barrels on overdrive &mdash; big, bold flavor in fewer years:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Garrison Brothers (Hye, TX)</strong> &mdash; the first legal bourbon distillery in Texas. Their Small Batch is thick, sweet, and unmistakably Texan; Balmorhea is the splurge.</li>
          <li><strong>Still Austin "The Musician" (Austin, TX)</strong> &mdash; grain-to-glass bourbon made right here in town from 100% Texas grain. Bright, youthful, and a fantastic local gift.</li>
          <li><strong>Balcones (Waco, TX)</strong> &mdash; the wild child of Texas whiskey. Baby Blue (blue corn) and Texas Single Malt are unlike anything else on the wall.</li>
          <li><strong>TX Whiskey (Fort Worth, TX)</strong> &mdash; smooth, approachable blended whiskey with a famous boot-leather-capped bottle.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Want to go deeper on local pours? Our <a href="/guides/texas-spirits-guide.html">Texas Spirits Guide</a> covers vodka, gin, and agave from around the state.</p>

        <h2>How to Choose</h2>
        <p>A quick cheat sheet from behind the counter:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Sipping neat?</strong> Look for age statements, bottled-in-bond, or single barrel picks.</li>
          <li><strong>Mixing cocktails?</strong> Higher proof (90+) holds up to ice and citrus. See our <a href="/guides/classic-cocktails-at-home.html">classic cocktail recipes</a> to put it to work.</li>
          <li><strong>Gifting?</strong> Texas bottles win every time &mdash; local story, beautiful packaging.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Still not sure? Come talk to us at either store &mdash; recommending the right bottle is genuinely our favorite part of the job.</p>
